# ── Internal, not published ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/architecture/ is public — it is the technical documentation, and it is
# the reason a stranger can tell this was built by people who understand it.
# The rest is the business of running the project, not of using the code:
# strategy, pricing, market sizing, competitor analysis, launch gates, and our
# own agent working agreements. Publishing those hands a stranger the pricing
# model and the roadmap. They stay on disk and stay versioned locally; they are
# simply not in this repository.
/docs/product/
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/product/CONTRIBUTING.md
/CLAUDE.md
# The pre-compaction CLAUDE.md (59k). Kept locally as the source the current
# one was cut from — every rule and measurement is still in docs/architecture/,
# which ships, so nothing is lost by ignoring this.
/CLAUDE.md.full
/CLAUDE.md.v[0-9]
/phase1.md

# Tracking is not the same as publishing, and the two used to be conflated —
# the failure was silent in both directions. A new doc under docs/product/ used
# to be a no-op to `git add`, so a launch-gating document could go unwritten
# from the team's point of view. The fix is scoping, not blanket ignoring: one
# tree ships, the other does not.

# The old note this replaced, kept because the history matters: /docs/ and
# /CLAUDE.md were ignored here while 27 files under docs/ were already tracked
# (force-added), which made the lines inert for existing files and actively
# harmful for new ones — a doc could be local-only unless you remembered
# `git add -f`, including release-plan.md and cws-submission.md, which gate the
# Chrome Web Store submission. A `git add -f` also leaves the file tracked
# forever, so the ignore rule stops meaning anything for it.

# Six files were in exactly that state and have been untracked with
# `git rm --cached` — still on disk, no longer in history:
#   .superpowers/…/task-3-report.md   an AI-dev task report
#   PLAN.md, decisions.md              the build plan and the D1–D10 lock record
#   clients/…/preview.html, .preview/  local panel previews
# The reasoning behind D1–D10 now lives in docs/architecture/, which ships.
/PLAN.md
/decisions.md
/clients/brotto-extension/preview.html

# Local agent config — absolute paths and per-machine permissions.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Third-party agent skills, vendored by `npx skills add <org>/<repo>`. Remotion's
# is ~19k lines of upstream documentation that we did not write and do not edit;
# it belongs to whoever installed it, at whatever version they installed. The
# lockfile goes with them — it pins a tool's install, not a dependency of ours.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
skills-lock.json

# Local scratch previews
.preview/

# Visual brainstorming companion
.superpowers/

# Rendered videos. The .txt stays — it is a deliverable; the mp4 does not belong in history.
brag-output/*.mp4
